SPARTA (24 Sep 2025)
Running on 1 MPI task(s)
################################################################################
# thermal gas in a closed 3d box
#
# Regression coverage for two commands/fixes not used by any other example:
#   scale_particles - clone the particle population by a fixed factor
#   fix halt        - monitor an equal-style variable each N steps
# The box is closed (reflecting walls) so the particle count stays constant and
# the halt condition (np < 8000) is evaluated every 100 steps but never trips,
# exercising the fix halt setup and periodic check for the full run.
#
# Note:
#  - The "comm/sort" option to the "global" command is used to match MPI runs.
#  - The "twopass" option is used to match Kokkos runs.
# The "comm/sort" and "twopass" options should not be used for production runs.
################################################################################

seed	    	    12345
dimension   	    3
global              gridcut 1.0e-5 comm/sort yes

boundary	    r r r

create_box  	    0 0.0001 0 0.0001 0 0.0001
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (0.0001 0.0001 0.0001)
create_grid 	    10 10 10
Created 1000 child grid cells
  CPU time = 0.000963376 secs
  create/ghost percent = 80.3123 19.6877
balance_grid        rcb part
Balance grid migrated 0 cells
  CPU time = 0.000259046 secs
  reassign/sort/migrate/ghost percent = 59.0853 1.06313 12.8525 26.9991

species		    ar.species Ar
mixture		    air Ar vstream 0.0 0.0 0.0 temp 273.15

global              nrho 7.07043E22
global              fnum 7.07043E6

create_particles    air n 10000 twopass
Created 10000 particles
  CPU time = 0.0019298 secs

# clone the particle population by 1.5x
scale_particles     air 1.5
Scaled particles
  before = 10000, after = 15016
  CPU time = 0.000172589 secs

# monitor particle count; "error continue" keeps the run going after triggering
variable            pcount equal np
fix                 h halt 100 v_pcount < 8000 error continue

stats		    100
stats_style	    step cpu np
timestep 	    7.00E-9
run 		    1000
Memory usage per proc in Mbytes:
